  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Study Model on a Quiet Desk",
    "overview": "Etharic is one system with two registers. Every reading route (work, articles, about, 2026, contact) is a quiet desk: cool paper, graphite ink, hairline borders, Inter at reading sizes, one burnt-amber accent kept for the few actions that matter. The homepage sets a hand-built study model on that desk: four towers of cut white mount board on a basswood plate, lit by one raking light, one tower per audience. Both registers share the same ink, soft graphite, amber accent, hairlines and easing, so the model reads as an object placed on the site, not a second site.\n\nThe model is literal material, not illustration. Depth comes from three face fills of the same board (lit top, side, shade), from the plate's cut edge, and from a soft cast decal on the plate that skews with the light. At night (dark theme) the same model sits in a dim studio: board faces drop to graphite, basswood darkens, and only the selected tower's windows glow amber. Choosing an audience raises that tower one course, lights it, swings the light and turns the plate.\n\nThe voice is personal and playful (lowercase copy, a pixel dog, a live clock) but the surfaces are restrained. Rejected: corporate polish, glossy 3D blobs, glass, decorative gradients and glow halos.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat tonal surfaces with 1px hairlines; no elevation shadows on reading routes.",
      "One accent (burnt amber) for the primary action of a view; one decorative amber (window glow) inside the model only.",
      "Inter for everything readable; Archivo expanded only for the homepage name and the plaques.",
      "The homepage model is built from real geometry: 28px courses, three face shades, a perspective plate.",
      "Motion is short, ease-out and transform/opacity only; reduced motion keeps crossfades and drops movement."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Amber Rule",
        "body": "Burnt amber marks at most one or two actions per view. If a second thing wants amber, it gets graphite ink instead.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Raking Light Rule",
        "body": "Model faces use exactly the three mount-board shades, lit top, side, shade, in that order. Depth in the model never comes from box-shadow or gradients.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Night Studio Rule",
        "body": "Dark theme does not invert the model; it dims it. Faces go to graphite, basswood darkens, windows keep the same amber.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Archivo Fence Rule",
        "body": "Archivo appears only on the homepage name and the plaques. Any other text, including the homepage intro, is Inter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Material Depth Rule",
        "body": "If something looks raised, it is because it is built in 3D or has a lighter tone, not because it casts a box-shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every color from the tokens, with a dark value for each surface color.",
      "Do keep burnt amber to one or two actions per view (get cv; the picked intro link).",
      "Do build model depth from the three mount-board shades, the basswood edge and the cast decal.",
      "Do animate only transform and opacity with `--ease-out` (`cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)`), 160 to 420ms; keep a 200ms crossfade under reduced motion.",
      "Do keep touch targets at 44px minimum and a 2px graphite ink focus ring on every control.",
      "Do keep Archivo inside the Archivo fence (homepage name, plaques)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use box-shadows, glass, glow halos or decorative gradients to suggest depth.",
      "Don't let the model take more than half the viewport width on desktop, or run an animation loop while idle, on touch, or in a hidden tab.",
      "Don't light more than one tower; the other three stay plain card.",
      "Don't model a real Frankfurt building; the towers stay abstract.",
      "Don't use signal green for anything but the theme switch and the status dot."
    ]
  }
